      "value": "@{632a1f5ab98aa644af84dab3|full_name}: could caching the performance level, be done together with the image and name caching, then have set in the api when uploading an avi, and for avies that have not been loaded have it store it locally when you first look at the avie in the inspector. for the sorting you would then just put all the unknowns last in alphabetical order.\n\nno idea about the real complexaty here, but this would atleast be one of the way where i could see this being pulled off. in a usefull but not perfect manner",
